"comparison": "Both Micron and Broadcom (AVGO) identify price erosion and declines in average selling prices as characteristic features of semiconductor industry down-cycles that reduce profitability. Micron highlights that its ASPs have ranged from positive low-teens to negative high-50% over five years, causing adverse effects when they decline faster than costs. AVGO notes that historical down-cycles have been characterized by 'accelerated erosion of average selling prices,' leading to reduced profitability, and warns that supply increases (including from the CHIPS Act) could further decrease ASPs.",
